{"h":3395,"lines":[{"y":0.11126028432169544,"w":0.072704092661539765,"h":0.014885848486802522,"c":1,"t":"Reading","x":0.83922577647028007},{"x":0.18518518882377455,"c":1,"w":0.69958847045898431,"t":"Dr Jenny Gibson agrees, pointing out that although some of the steps in the puzzle of how and","h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.15253239097481885},{"x":0.18106996315009108,"w":0.69341562906901055,"c":1,"y":0.1686046510164223,"t":"why play is important have been looked at, there is very little data on the impact it has on the","h":0.016024324441826665},{"t":"child's later life.","x":0.18069233060600132,"c":1,"w":0.12435302734374998,"y":0.18380699163179703,"h":0.015528398071217198},{"h":0.017345783426848671,"t":"Now, thanks to the university's new Centre for Research on Play in Education, Development and","y":0.21364097961247952,"w":0.69969904581705744,"x":0.18102056101554989,"c":1},{"x":0.18101650214893672,"y":0.22944355401015137,"h":0.016531005203372917,"c":1,"w":0.72438735961914058,"t":"Learning (PEDAL), Whitebread, Baker, Gibson and a team of researchers hope to provide evidence"},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"on the role played by play in how a child develops.","y":0.2470553591765039,"c":1,"w":0.3683127593994141,"x":0.18312757081263867},{"c":1,"y":0.27616279055155291,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"'A strong possibility is that play supports the early development of children's self-control,'","x":0.18106995780295543,"w":0.67283950805664061},{"y":0.29210836302579313,"x":0.18312756187263404,"t":"explains Baker. 'This is our ability to develop awareness of our own thinking processes - it","w":0.67695475260416671,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1},{"w":0.5534979248046874,"h":0.014574259835502645,"c":1,"x":0.18312758113398103,"y":0.30668604636703678,"t":"influences how effectively we go about undertaking challenging activities?'"},{"w":0.70587351481119787,"h":0.017129980633199926,"c":1,"x":0.17896483375347713,"t":"In a study carried out by Baker with toddlers and young pre-schoolers, she found that children with","y":0.33702223694802202},{"y":0.35261638541172624,"h":0.017590430656226452,"c":1,"x":0.1809852897537822,"t":"greater self-control solved problems more quickly when exploring an unfamiliar set-up requiring","w":0.68739593505859387},{"h":0.017960481003400752,"t":"scientific reasoningẠỊThis sort of evidence makes us think that giving children the chance to play will","y":0.36759578416461258,"w":0.71825719197591154,"c":1,"x":0.18099959570100982},{"h":0.016010694425153793,"x":0.18099642810890487,"c":1,"t":"make them more successful problem-solvers in the long run?","w":0.43638188680013018,"y":0.38368350813588736},{"x":0.18102855979705415,"h":0.015890726913973308,"y":0.41404912124467297,"c":1,"w":0.69762517293294268,"t":"If playful experiences do facilitate this aspect of development, say the researchers, it could be"},{"x":0.18099164459454242,"y":0.42850741671088899,"w":0.67916025797526047,"h":0.01802310954836428,"c":1,"t":"extremely significant for educational practices, because the ability to self-regulate has been"},{"h":0.016662762780071505,"y":0.4449052209329718,"c":1,"x":0.18098334028681393,"t":"shown to be a key predictor of academic performance.","w":0.40757502237955723},{"y":0.47518856608901006,"t":"Gibson adds: 'Playful behaviour is also an important indicator of healthy social and emotional","x":0.18102409216053295,"h":0.017307106260697314,"w":0.70380711873372392,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"development. In my previous research, I investigated how observing children at play can","x":0.18312758195252543,"w":0.65637858072916666,"y":0.49263839812628174,"h":0.013250883392226132},{"y":0.50578447867558529,"c":1,"x":0.18303985990390781,"h":0.016703957242033329,"w":0.65861638387044275,"t":"give us important clues about their well-being and can even be useful in the diagnosis of"},{"c":1,"x":0.18093018946616013,"y":0.52174642443505637,"h":0.01660318902580693,"t":"neurodevelopmental disorders like autism.'","w":0.32334609985351559},{"w":0.67499537150065103,"t":"Whitebread's recent research has involved developing a play-based approach to supporting","h":0.017451071767279003,"c":1,"y":0.55226040619168404,"x":0.18102383696327687},{"c":1,"y":0.56772510424708944,"t":"children's writing. 'Many primary school children find writing difficult, but we showed in a","x":0.18099914551211166,"h":0.017347753679794464,"w":0.67915512084960938},{"c":1,"h":0.01727578777587313,"x":0.18097721953890888,"w":0.71619695027669272,"y":0.5821786434120203,"t":"previous study that a playful stimulus was far more effective than an instructional one.' Children"},{"y":0.59875912187759506,"x":0.18101157024659925,"c":1,"w":0.65237792968750008,"h":0.017165640077265176,"t":"wrote longer and better-structured stories when they first played with dolls representing"},{"y":0.61336866885660213,"h":0.017445284008839379,"t":"characters in the story. In the latest study, children first created their story with Lego*, with","w":0.67901234944661448,"c":1,"x":0.18106996411414117},{"t":"similar results. 'Many teachers commented that they had always previously had children saying","w":0.70996943155924486,"x":0.18101967971951732,"h":0.017255081585635823,"c":1,"y":0.62929384577320613},{"t":"they didn't know what to write about. With the Lego building, however, not a single child said","h":0.017627978914618092,"c":1,"y":0.64504885093920217,"w":0.69971084594726574,"x":0.18101873782397462},{"x":0.17901234768459054,"y":0.66133720914233396,"t":"this through the whole year of the project.?'","w":0.32098765055338541,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"w":0.70795247395833327,"y":0.6905517832644511,"c":1,"x":0.18100158161412405,"h":0.018105903418802582,"t":"Whitebread, who directs PEDAL, trained as a primary school teacher in the early 1970s, when,"},{"x":0.17901234526316367,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"t":"as he describes, 'the teaching of young children was largely a quiet backwater, untroubled by any","y":0.70784883706303847,"w":0.72427983601888024},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"t":"serious intellectual debate or controversy? Now, the landscape is very different, with hotly debated","w":0.73251027425130211,"y":0.7208480566848019,"x":0.17901235505541885},{"t":"topics such as school starting age.","x":0.17883934443013552,"y":0.73829511528466829,"w":0.25962295532226565,"h":0.016420787299058492,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"'Somehow the importance of play has been lost in recent decades. It's regarded as something","x":0.18100860219819878,"y":0.7674238747023906,"w":0.68941889444986981,"h":0.016978325636002101},{"c":1,"x":0.18106994981869984,"y":0.78343023242097698,"t":"trivial, or even as something negative that contrasts with \"work\". Let's not lose sight of its","h":0.014567411690072807,"w":0.67078191121419273},{"x":0.18106996805436562,"y":0.79941860450629765,"w":0.72016459147135414,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"benefits, and the fundamental contributions it makes to human achievements in the arts, sciences","c":1},{"y":0.81245645134309263,"w":0.58053146362304686,"h":0.019891181739115193,"x":0.18096334780755663,"c":1,"t":"and technology. Let's make sure children have a rich diet of play experiences.?'"},{"t":"* Lego: coloured plastic building blocks and other pieces that can be joined together","y":0.84008859348886422,"h":0.013060501242414091,"w":0.44250381469726563,"c":1,"x":0.18099213481813195},{"c":1,"y":0.86773255842010921,"t":"17","w":0.024691357612609877,"x":0.88683127592620548,"h":0.013081394460653373}],"w":2400}